<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document>
<name>Unsleeping City walking tour: Chapter 2</name>
<description>Halloween to the holidays, three years on: dragons, devils, a stolen city and an egg about to hatch.</description>
<Folder><name>Day 1: The Dragon's downtown</name>
<Placemark><name>1. Battery Park &amp; Castle Clinton</name><description>When the party decides to strike at Ellis Island, a ferry is waiting for Kingston, the Vox Populi, piloted by his bus driver turned captain (Ep. 14). Next door at Whitehall Terminal, the group meets to take the Staten Island Ferry to the monastery; Pete makes it just as the boat departs (Ep. 6).

Visiting: Ferry tickets for the Statue of Liberty and Ellis Island are sold at Castle Clinton and online. There is airport-style security before boarding, so arrive early. The free Staten Island Ferry leaves from Whitehall Terminal, a few minutes' walk east.

Scenes: C2E14-S10, C2E06-S06, C2E06-S07</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0166,40.7035,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Ellis Island</name><description>The chapter's big set piece. In the story the museum is closed, chained and being sold to Gladiator. Null strips the heroes of parts of themselves, and they dive into historic photographs in the Great Hall to win them back (Ep. 14). Null erases Iga from time, and a drawing of Holly Branch, with a fragment of the Fairyland sign, opens the way to Faerie (Ep. 15).

Visiting: The National Museum of Immigration fills the main building, and the Great Hall is on the second floor. Boats from Battery Park stop at Liberty Island first. Allow at least three hours for the round trip.

Scenes: C2E14-S11, C2E14-S12, C2E14-S13, C2E14-S14, C2E14-S15, C2E14-S16, C2E15-S01, C2E15-S02</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0396,40.6995,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. 9/11 Memorial &amp; Museum</name><description>In Nod, the party finds a Latin inscription on a marble civic building: 'Nulla dies umquam memori vos eximet aevo.' From it, Pete's True Sight wins the enemy's name: Null (Ep. 10). In the waking world, the English version of that line from Virgil's Aeneid ('No day shall erase you from the memory of time') is inscribed in the 9/11 Memorial Museum.

Visiting: The memorial pools are free and open to all. The museum, where the quotation hangs in Memorial Hall, is ticketed. Please be respectful: this is a memorial.

Scenes: C2E10-S06</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0133,40.7114,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. City Hall &amp; the old City Hall station</name><description>Where Kingston's story starts. In a 1994 flashback, young Kingston takes a call at a payphone on Lafayette St, wanders into the abandoned City Hall station, and finds the dying Dragon of Bleecker Street in a treasure-lined burrow. The dragon makes him the Vox Populi, gives him a subway token, and vanishes as a 4 train pulls into Brooklyn Bridge-City Hall (Ep. 1). Years later Kingston goes back to the same payphone to call for help (Ep. 13). The courthouses on Foley Square, just north, are the marble Civic Center that Nod mirrors in Episode 10.

Visiting: The old City Hall station closed in 1945, but you can still glimpse it: stay aboard a downtown 6 after its last stop at Brooklyn Bridge-City Hall, and the train loops through the old station before heading back uptown.

Scenes: C2E01-S01, C2E01-S02, C2E01-S03, C2E13-S03</description><Point><coordinates>-74.005,40.7128,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Chinatown: Mott Street</name><description>The Shen family, draconic sorcerers, live behind a Mott Street door that opens onto an extra-dimensional mountain bridge. They brought the Dragon of Bleecker Street's egg to New York in the 1870s, and they give the party medicines and lore for raising a dragon (Ep. 13). Later Cody rides his moped around Chinatown and Bleecker St hunting for the hidden hoard (Ep. 15).

Visiting: The party walks in past Columbus Park, where mornings are busy with tai chi and card games. A good place for lunch.

Scenes: C2E13-S07, C2E15-S06</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9983,40.7157,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. The Holland Tunnel &amp; the Hudson</name><description>Looking across the Hudson, Ricky and Cody see storm clouds massing over New Jersey: the Jersey Devil and his Shore buddies are coming through the tunnel (Ep. 4). The party meets at the Manhattan mouth of the tunnel, where the Questing Blade chooses Cody and becomes a greatsword (Ep. 5), before the fight under the river.

Visiting: The walk here along Canal and Broome Sts passes the tunnel's entrance plaza. The squat building out on the water at Pier 34 is one of the tunnel's ventilation towers. The tunnel itself is closed to people on foot.

Scenes: C2E04-S10, C2E05-S04, C2E05-S05</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0124,40.7262,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. West 4th St station &amp; Bleecker Street</name><description>The 'confluence' of anti-social magic that the demon Bazathrax warns about. The new party assembles on this platform for the first time; a haunted express train skips the stop, and they all leap aboard (Ep. 2). It becomes a runaway northbound A train full of graves, which Ricky stops near the end of the line, at Dyckman St (Ep. 3). Bleecker Street, which gave the dragon its name, crosses 6th Ave just south of here.

Visiting: It's a two-level station: the A, C and E on one level, the B, D, F and M on the other. To follow the runaway train, take an uptown A to Dyckman St, the second-to-last stop (about 35 minutes). Washington Square Park is a block east.

Scenes: C2E02-S13, C2E03-S01, C2E03-S02</description><Point><coordinates>-74.0004,40.7321,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
