</Folder>
<Folder><name>Day 2: Midtown to the Hoard</name>
<Placemark><name>1. Herald Square &amp; the parade route</name><description>Thanksgiving: the party is watching the Macy's parade from the crowd when true clowns from the Dreaming knock out Wally Claus, cut the lines and fly off on four giant balloons. The fight continues in the air over Midtown (Ep. 7).

Visiting: The real parade ends here at Macy's on Thanksgiving morning. The story never says where the party stands.

Scenes: C2E07-S04, C2E07-S05</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9884,40.7506,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Empire State Building</name><description>In Nod, the top of the Empire State Building is where Pete finds a hole leaking raw Umbra into the Dreaming (Eps. 6 and 7). Iga's family chest carves a picture of Sofia and Ricky on top of the building (Eps. 1 and 4).

Visiting: The observation decks on the 86th and 102nd floors are ticketed. For a free view of the spire, look up from 5th Ave at 33rd St.

Scenes: C2E06-S04, C2E07-S02, C2E01-S18, C2E04-S01</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9857,40.7484,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. New York Public Library (Stephen A. Schwarzman Building)</name><description>The Gramercy Occult Society, hidden behind the lions, is the chapter's nerve center. Esther's rune map raises the alarm about the Holland Tunnel (Ep. 5), and JJ moves in and builds a time-travel watch (Ep. 14). In 'Treachery at Gramercy' the party fights Tony Simos in the Umbral Engine chamber beneath the library (Ep. 16), where Dale comes back to life (Ep. 17).

Visiting: Free to enter during opening hours. Don't miss the Rose Main Reading Room on the third floor. The show calls the lions Orlando and Rovias; their real names are Patience and Fortitude.

Scenes: C2E04-S09, C2E05-S01, C2E06-S15, C2E08-S05, C2E14-S09, C2E15-S15, C2E16-S01, C2E17-S01</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9817,40.7531,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Grand Central Terminal</name><description>The party whispers into the corners of the Whispering Gallery to summon the clock gnomes. The gnomes shrink everyone into a matchbox and lend them a tiny dragon-headed train that runs on the pipes through the subway to the Bronx (Ep. 11).

Visiting: The Whispering Gallery is outside the Oyster Bar on the lower level: stand in opposite corners of the arches and whisper into the wall.

Scenes: C2E11-S08</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9772,40.7527,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Upper West Side: W 72nd Street</name><description>Iga's day job is 'Madam Anastasia', a half-basement psychic shop on W 72nd near Columbus Ave. She reads Sofia's tarot (the Tower, the Three of Wands), and a customer named Yagdash, bringing drug money to launder, shoots himself in the backside (Ep. 1).

Visiting: The shop is fictional, but the block is full of half-basement storefronts like it. The Dakota stands at the corner of W 72nd St and Central Park West, on the way into the park.

Scenes: C2E01-S09</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9786,40.7776,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Central Park: the Carousel</name><description>The chapter's last scene: two or three years on, everyone meets for a huge family barbecue in Central Park, by the carousel the new mayor saved (Ep. 18). Earlier, Ricky trains by swinging through the park's trees like monkey bars (Ep. 6).

Visiting: The carousel sits in the middle of the park at about 65th St.

Scenes: C2E18-S04, C2E06-S11</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9752,40.7699,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. The Met: Arms and Armor</name><description>Nod's mirror of the Met, the Metropolitan Museum of Memories, hosts the Fight at the Museum. In the Arms and Armor wing the party frees the chained Unicorn of New York from animated suits of armor, and Cody fuses Excalibur with his Thirsting Blade (Ep. 9). Deeper in, the Hall of Memories reveals the erasing entity that took earlier Voxes Phantasma (Ep. 10).

Visiting: Admission is ticketed. The Arms and Armor galleries, with their mounted knights, are on the first floor.

Scenes: C2E09-S06, C2E10-S01, C2E10-S02</description><Point><coordinates>-73.963,40.779,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Central Park North: 110th Street</name><description>The finale. The Dragon of Bleecker Street's hoard has been moved under this station and hidden by the Umbral Arcana, until Kingston finally recognizes the way down (Eps. 15 and 17). Below, the egg hatches, the party defeats Null, Iga breaks back into time, and the newborn dragon Langston becomes Kingston and Liz's son (Eps. 17 and 18).

Visiting: The 2 and 3 trains stop at the corner of 110th St and Malcolm X Blvd. The walk here from the Met passes the Conservatory Garden and the Harlem Meer.

Scenes: C2E15-S11, C2E17-S03, C2E17-S04, C2E18-S01</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9519,40.7991,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Harlem: 125th Street</name><description>Kingston's block, now under threat. He lives in the family building with Liz, and St. Owen's, Cosmo's corner store and Pete's job at the Uncommon Knowledge bookstore are all just off 125th St. Reggie's electronics shop suddenly stands empty, and Excelsior Dynamic Homes is buying up the neighborhood (Eps. 1 and 4). The Browns host Thanksgiving for the party (Ep. 8).

Visiting: None of these places is a real address. The Apollo Theater is a few blocks west on 125th.

Scenes: C2E01-S06, C2E01-S11, C2E01-S12, C2E01-S13, C2E02-S11, C2E04-S07, C2E08-S07, C2E14-S02</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9453,40.8077,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
