<Folder><name>More places from the chapter</name>
<Placemark><name>Astoria</name><description>Pete and Cody's house share, the most-visited place in Chapter 2, is somewhere in Astoria, more than 20 minutes' walk from the subway. On Steinway St, Bazathrax bursts out of a smoking manhole (Ep. 2), and at the Neptune Diner, Maddie Park joins the fight against Gladiator (Ep. 14).

Visiting: The house is fictional and unlocated. Steinway St is a lively shopping street; start at the Steinway St station.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9208,40.7569,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Greenpoint: Manhattan Avenue</name><description>The Lisowski family home, where Iga keeps the ancient carved chest that holds a castle, and where her family cooks a huge Polish Thanksgiving in the castle's ovens (Ep. 8).

Visiting: The home is fictional. Manhattan Avenue is the heart of Greenpoint's Polish community, full of bakeries and delis.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.951,40.724,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Clinton Hill</name><description>Ricky and Esther now live above the Chantry, in a tall building with a miniature clock tower on top. The party plans its expedition into Nod at their loft (Eps. 8 and 9).

Visiting: Fictional. The brownstones along Clinton Avenue fit the neighborhood.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9665,40.6896,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Manhattan Bridge walkway</name><description>Sofia, newly a Shadow monk, hops across the rooftops from the Brooklyn end of the Manhattan Bridge toward Clinton Hill, breaking up a toxic couple on the way (Ep. 2).

Visiting: The bridge's walkway starts at Jay and Sands Sts in Brooklyn and has big views of the Brooklyn Bridge.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9869,40.7002,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Queens Center Mall (Fairyland)</name><description>Cody sells his soul in his old Hot Topic inside the shuttered mall to save it from Gladiator (Ep. 1). Gladiator builds its time-compression machine here, and in the epilogue Rowan's Fairyland reopens on part of the site (Ep. 18).

Visiting: A real, open shopping mall. It stands on the site of Fairyland, a real kiddie amusement park from the mid-20th century.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.87,40.7346,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Green-Wood Cemetery</name><description>At Dale's grave, Dale gives back the Questing Blade, disguised as nunchucks, and tells Sofia he'll stop visiting so she can live her life (Ep. 4).

Visiting: Free to visit. Enter at the Gothic main gate at 5th Ave and 25th St.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9945,40.6585,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Dyckman St station (A)</name><description>Where the runaway A train finally stops, the 'second to last station' on the line. Pete sees raw Umbral Arcana ebbing like a tide on the platform (Ep. 3).

Visiting: Fort Tryon Park and the Cloisters are a short walk south and uphill.</description><Point><coordinates>-73.9273,40.8655,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder></Document></kml>